# kyc-service CI checklist

Before pushing kyc-service changes, run scoped tests first; use full verify when touching shared config or migrations.

## Integration test support

- Use `KycIntegrationTestSupport` for `@SpringBootTest` — registers Postgres Testcontainer and shared test properties.
- AES test key must be **32 bytes**: `"test-aes-256-key-32-bytes-long!!"` (31-byte variant fails crypto init).

## Common CI failures

| Failure | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| MockMvc 500 on controller params | Explicit `@RequestParam(value = "...")`; parent `pom.xml` has `<parameters>true</parameters>` |
| Instant assertion mismatch | Re-fetch entity from repository after save — Postgres truncates microsecond precision |
| RabbitMQ listener startup in tests | Declare queues in `KycMessagingConfig`; set `spring.rabbitmq.listener.simple.auto-startup: false` in test YAML; mock `RabbitTemplate` where needed |
| Flyway migration conflict | Check existing `V*__*.sql` versions before adding (e.g. V1.3 taken → use V1.4) |
| JPA type mismatch | Flyway `NUMERIC` columns → `BigDecimal`, not `Double` |
| Scheduler deadlock | Do not hold `@Transactional` + `FOR UPDATE` across worker calls; split fetch into short `REQUIRES_NEW` transaction |

## Messaging / infra

- New RabbitMQ queues: add to `KycMessagingConfig` **and** `infra/docker/rabbitmq/definitions.json`.
